# Godot/GDScript Simulation Authority

The **Godot/GDScript simulation core** is the **single source of truth** for all gameplay rules. It is a pure GDScript layer (scripts/resources/classes) that is separate from UI scenes and rendering.

> Use the phrase "Godot/GDScript simulation core is authoritative" — never "Godot is authoritative." Scenes, rendering, and UI are **not** authoritative.

## Requirements

- The simulation core runs **headlessly** (Godot headless / no rendered scene required).
- All randomness comes from an explicit **seeded RNG** stored in simulation state.
- All authoritative, replay-hashed state uses **integers or fixed-point scaled integers** — never floats (see `.cursor/rules/02-` and `docs/architecture/05_`).
- All state changes emit **serializable events**.
- **Snapshots** are JSON-compatible and contain enough data for the Godot UI to render the game.
- **Commands** are validated and executed only in the simulation core.

## The simulation core MUST NOT depend on

- Scene tree state, Node or sprite positions
- Animation timing, frame delta (`_process`/`_physics_process` deltas), or wall-clock time
- Physics engine side effects, cameras, UI nodes, or input events

## Command Pipeline

All clients submit commands through the same path:

```
Client (UI / bot / agent / peer) → CommandValidator → Simulation Core → Events + Snapshot
```

Clients include: human (via Godot UI), bots, neural agents, future multiplayer peers.

## Python role

Python is **training and tooling only** (neural training, analysis, tournament processing, CSV/JSON tools, batch workflows). Python is **not** the shipped authoritative runtime and is **not** embedded in the mobile app. Python training reaches the sim by running Godot headless (see `docs/architecture/04_bot_and_training_architecture.md`).

## Forbidden in UI / scene / rendering code

- Authoritative gameplay rules (damage, production, pathfinding, economy)
- Random number generation for gameplay outcomes
- Direct state mutation bypassing the command pipeline
- Using float animation/presentation values as authoritative state

The Godot visual client may: display snapshots, collect input, serialize commands, show diagnostics.

See `docs/architecture/01_simulation_core_authoritative.md`.
